    <h2>1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p>The Queen Dairy Menu (thequeendairymenu.us) is an independent, privately operated reference website that publishes publicly available information about the Dairy Queen® menu, including estimated prices, calories, and product details. We are the “data controller” for the limited information described in this policy. <strong>We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Dairy Queen®, International Dairy Queen, Inc., or any of their subsidiaries.</strong></p>

    <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
    <h3>2a. Information you provide</h3>
    <p>No account is required to use this website. If you contact us through our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, we collect the name, email address, and message content you voluntarily provide. This is used solely to respond to your inquiry and is not sold or used for marketing.</p>
    <h3>2b. Information collected automatically</h3>
    <p>When you visit the site, standard web technologies automatically collect limited technical data:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Log data</strong> — IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URL, pages viewed, and date/time of visit.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies and identifiers</strong> — small files and identifiers used for functionality, analytics, and advertising (see Sections 5–7).</li>
      <li><strong>Device information</strong> — approximate screen size, browser version, and device type (desktop, mobile, tablet).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect sensitive personal information such as financial account numbers, health data, precise geolocation, or government ID numbers.</p>

    <h2>3. How We Use Information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To operate and display the website correctly on your device;</li>
      <li>To measure traffic and understand how visitors use our content (analytics);</li>
      <li>To display advertising, including personalized ads where permitted (see Section 6);</li>
      <li>To respond to contact-form messages;</li>
      <li>To maintain security and to keep our menu information accurate and up to date.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell or rent your personal information, and we do not use it to build profiles beyond what the analytics and advertising services described below provide.</p>

    <h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing (EEA/UK Visitors)</h2>
    <p>If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we process your information on these legal bases under the GDPR/UK GDPR: <strong>consent</strong> (for advertising and analytics cookies, where required, which you may withdraw at any time); <strong>legitimate interests</strong> (operating, securing, and improving the site in a way that does not override your rights); and, for contact-form messages, taking <strong>steps at your request</strong>. Where consent is the basis, you may withdraw it without affecting prior processing.</p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
    <p>We and our service providers use the following categories of cookies:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Functional</strong> — remember basic preferences such as navigation state and session continuity.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — Google Analytics cookies that collect aggregated, de-identified usage data (see Section 7).</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising</strong> — cookies set by Google and its partners to serve and measure ads (see Section 6).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can control or delete cookies through your browser settings. Disabling cookies may affect some site features. For a general overview of managing cookies, see <a href="https://www.aboutcookies.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutcookies.org</a>.</p>

    <h2>6. Advertising — Google AdSense &amp; Third-Party Vendors</h2>
    <p>This website displays advertising served through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>. In connection with this:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Third-party vendors, <strong>including Google</strong>, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to this website and other websites.</li>
      <li>Google's use of advertising cookies — including the <strong>DoubleClick DART cookie</strong> — enables it and its partners to serve ads to you based on your visits to this and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
      <li>You may <strong>opt out of personalized advertising</strong> by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>. You can also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info/choices</a> and <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">optout.networkadvertising.org</a>.</li>
      <li>Where required by law (for example, for EEA, UK, and Swiss users), Google and its partners obtain consent for the use of advertising cookies in line with Google's EU user consent policy.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For details on how Google uses information from sites that use its services, see <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services</a>, and review <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Privacy Policy</a>. A current list of Google's advertising technology providers is available in your Google ad settings. We do not control, and are not responsible for, the data practices of third-party advertisers.</p>

    <h2>7. Analytics</h2>
    <p>We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to measure traffic and understand how visitors use our content. Google Analytics uses cookies to collect aggregated, de-identified information such as pages viewed and general location. You can opt out across all sites by installing the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics Opt-out Browser Add-on</a>.</p>

    <h2>8. Your Privacy Rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have some or all of the following rights over your personal information:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the data we hold about you;</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — request that we delete your data;</li>
      <li><strong>Correction</strong> — request correction of inaccurate data;</li>
      <li><strong>Portability</strong> — request your data in a portable format;</li>
      <li><strong>Object / restrict</strong> — object to or restrict certain processing;</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out</strong> — opt out of personalized advertising (Section 6).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. We will respond to verified requests within 30 days (or 45 days where a longer period is permitted by law). You will not be treated differently for exercising your rights.</p>

    <h2>9. EEA/UK (GDPR) Users</h2>
    <p>If you are in the EEA or UK, you also have the right to <strong>lodge a complaint with your local data protection supervisory authority</strong> if you believe our processing is unlawful. We encourage you to contact us first so we can address your concern.</p>

    <h2>10. California Residents (CCPA/CPRA)</h2>
    <p>Under the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the CPRA, California residents have the right to know what personal information is collected, to request access and deletion, to correct inaccurate information, and to opt out of the “sale” or “sharing” of personal information. <strong>We do not sell your personal information for money.</strong> Please note that the use of advertising cookies for cross-context behavioral advertising (Section 6) may be considered “sharing” under California law; you can opt out using the personalized-advertising controls in Section 6 or by using the Global Privacy Control (GPC) signal, which we honor where technically feasible. To submit a request, use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. We will not discriminate against you for exercising these rights.</p>

    <h2>11. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain contact-form messages for up to 12 months to manage correspondence. Server log data is retained for up to 90 days. Analytics data is retained per Google Analytics default retention settings (up to 26 months). We delete or de-identify data when it is no longer needed.</p>

    <h2>12. Data Security</h2>
    <p>The site is served over encrypted HTTPS, and we apply reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect the limited information we hold. However, no method of transmission or storage over the Internet is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h2>13. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>Our service providers (such as Google) may process information in the United States and other countries. Where required, these transfers rely on appropriate safeguards such as the providers' standard contractual clauses. By using the site, you understand your information may be processed outside your country of residence.</p>

    <h2>14. Do Not Track</h2>
    <p>Some browsers offer a “Do Not Track” (DNT) setting. Because there is no common industry standard for responding to DNT signals, we do not currently respond to them. You can still control advertising and analytics as described in Sections 6 and 7, and we honor the Global Privacy Control where feasible.</p>

    <h2>15. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>This website is intended for a general audience and is <strong>not directed to children under 13</strong> (or the equivalent minimum age in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you are a parent or guardian and believe your child has provided us information, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we will promptly delete it.</p>

    <h2>16. External Links</h2>
    <p>Our site links to external websites, including the official Dairy Queen website and social platforms. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or content of those sites, and we encourage you to review their policies.</p>

    <h2>17. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be posted here with a new effective date. Continued use of the site after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

    <h2>18. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this Privacy Policy or your data? Please use our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. For more about who runs this site, see our <a href="/about">About page</a> and <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>. To return to the menu, visit <a href="/">The Dairy Queen Menu</a>.</p>
  
